# EF Core / SQL Server

- `HmaDbContext` implements `IHmaDbContext`. Application code depends on the interface, not the context type.
- Tables and columns: English PascalCase, singular table names, PK `Id`, FK `{Table}Id`, freight money `decimal(20,2)`, frozen accounting money `decimal(18,0)`, text `nvarchar`, dates `datetime2`.
- Do not reintroduce legacy names (`nil`, `kh_ud`, `sopc_ud`) as production identifiers. Keep `LegacyId` only for ETL.
- Configure mappings in `OnModelCreating` (or dedicated `IEntityTypeConfiguration<T>` in its own file). Do not use Plexis/`ui_engine_*` tables.
- `Include` navigations the use case needs; no lazy loading. Paginate or `Take` list queries.
- Schema changes are **code-first**: entity + `OnModelCreating`, then `dotnet ef migrations add <Name> --project src/Hma.Infrastructure.SqlServer`. App startup runs `HmaDatabaseInitializer.MigrateAndSeedAsync` (`Database.Migrate`). Do not add ad-hoc `ALTER` in `PatchSchema` / `EnsureCreated`. Keep `database/001_schema.sql` aligned for ETL/cutover.
- New migration command (repo root, after `dotnet tool restore`):
  `dotnet ef migrations add <Name> --project src/Hma.Infrastructure.SqlServer --output-dir Migrations`
- Auth: hash passwords (PBKDF2). Never persist plaintext. Seed and migrations must not copy `legacy` `[user].password` as-is into production login.
